Could You Beat an Ice Age Predator? — an Art Deco film (10 min)

Script and voiceover: supplied by the user (recorded with ElevenLabs, voice "Peter – Youthful and Expressive").
The voice is used as supplied; the film only levels it. The script's last two lines are not in the recording
and appear as title cards.

Picture: everything drawn in code (Canvas2D), no generated images, no third-party artwork.
Animals drawn from published body proportions; the Chauvet-style lions are our own drawings, not tracings.
Drawing engine adapted from the library's Art Deco style tools.

